From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: checker fixes to 0984 (zortos293/Lichii #1520) and 0985 (#1585), off unless set

Fixes found in review of T182c (read in source; compile-checked, not run). Credits as 0984/0985:
zortos293/Lichii #1520 (8dcea11) and #1585 (19ae2d1), Zortos.

- EDEN_UP_L1585_STATE_BLOCKS: the front worked out the fast draw check with
  Maxwell3D::IsFastDrawParameter, whose EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW branch (IsL1161VertexFormat) also sets
  Nx2FastDraw::g_delta.vertex_formats_changed: a plain bool of the back's, written from the front
  thread out of stream order, and never set by the back for a block it stores at once (with
  EDEN_UP_L1161_DRAW switched off live in between, a delta draw could keep stale vertex input).
  Now the front asks without the side effect (IsFastDrawParameter(method, false)) and marks a
  State entry holding a vertex attribute format word (HasVertexFormat, bit 5 of the head); the
  back, storing such a block at once with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW on, runs the check for those words
  as WriteDirtyRegister would. Upstream has the same front call.
- EDEN_UP_L1520_ASYNC_COPY: one line at the first channel saying whether it can act. It only
  acts at resumes that refresh the queued lists: EDEN_NX2_RESNAPSHOT on and EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT,
  EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX, EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY all 0. The play settings have
  EDEN_NX2_RESNAPSHOT=0 and EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT=1: there it says IDLE and does nothing.
- EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL: one line at the first channel with its state and cap.

Unset: nothing here runs or prints. No file here is a translation id input and no name is added
to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
index b5f44e75be..764b81e1a4 100644
--- a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
@@ -1060,6 +1060,26 @@ DmaPusher::DmaPusher(Core::System& system_, MemoryManager& memory_manager_, Cont
             KeepCopyParserClash(SplitCheckMode());
         }
     }
+    // EDEN_UP_L1520_ASYNC_COPY / _WORDS_POOL (0986): proves each switch was read, and says when
+    // ASYNC_COPY cannot act (its count line comes only from resumes that refresh the lists).
+    if (static std::atomic<bool> reported{}; AsyncCopyEnabled() && !reported.exchange(true)) {
+        const bool idle = !ResnapshotEnabled() || FetchCountMode() != 0 ||
+                          DesyncFixMode() != 0 || ResumeKeepCopyMode() != 0;
+        LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU,
+                    "EDEN_UP_L1520_ASYNC_COPY=1 {}: EDEN_NX2_RESNAPSHOT {}, EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT={}, "
+                    "EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX={}, EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY={} (it acts only with "
+                    "RESNAPSHOT on and the other three 0; DESYNC_FIX and KEEP_COPY also by title)",
+                    idle ? "IDLE" : "on", ResnapshotEnabled() ? "on" : "=0", FetchCountMode(),
+                    DesyncFixMode(), ResumeKeepCopyMode());
+    }
+    if (static std::atomic<bool> reported{};
+        std::getenv("EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL") != nullptr && !reported.exchange(true)) {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL");
+        LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL={} ({}): at most {} MiB of free command "
+                            "word blocks kept (EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL_MIB)",
+                    value, CommandWordsPool::PoolEnabled() ? "on" : "off",
+                    CommandWordsPool::PoolCapBytes() >> 20);
+    }
 }
 
 DmaPusher::~DmaPusher() {
